PS5 HDMI: 100 Hz modes, test

FLAVA3 only, each offered only when the display goes to 100 Hz or more and its clock limit
allows; no new options:
 - 1440p100: CVT reduced blanking (410.5 MHz, 2720x1510, standard 1440p sync shape), between
   1440p60 and 1440p120, which already share the chip's 1440p index 0x04
 - 1080p100 (VIC 64): the chip gets the VIC for 1080p, as for 1080p60 (16) and 1080p120 (63);
   whether its firmware has VIC 64 is what this test finds out
 - 4K100 (VIC 117, when the display lists it): Sony's index 0x0a over FRL, through the 4K120
   guard (only where FRL can work) and fallback (back to 4K by itself if the link fails)
---

--- a/drivers/ps5/hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/ps5/hdmi.c
